Lipflow bundles code from these projects:

- espnet/ — a trimmed copy of ESPnet (Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2017 Johns Hopkins
  University and ESPnet contributors), as vendored by Auto-AVSR and Chaplin. Lipflow patches:
  distutils removed (Python 3.12+), device-agnostic CTC prefix scoring, and cached cross-attention
  keys/values during beam search.
- lipflow/mean_face.npy, lipflow/unigram5000_units.txt and the preprocessing in lipflow/face.py
  and lipflow/vsr.py are adapted from Auto-AVSR / Visual_Speech_Recognition_for_Multiple_Languages
  by Pingchuan Ma et al., Imperial College London (Apache License 2.0).
- lipflow/data/web2-lower.txt.gz — the lowercase words of web2 (Webster's Second International,
  1934, public domain; the /usr/share/dict/words list on macOS and BSD), so name snapping can tell
  real words from names on Windows too.
- Chaplin by Amanvir Parhar (MIT License) — the original "type what you mouth" idea and the
  Hugging Face mirrors of the model weights.

Model weights (downloaded by setup.sh, not redistributed here) are the Auto-AVSR LRS3 models; the
LRS3 dataset is licensed for non-commercial research use, so treat the weights the same way.

Optional Mandarin support:
- scripts/fetch_chinese_lips.py retrieves a deterministic subset of the authors'
  processed Chinese-LiPS face videos and metadata from the pinned BAAI release:
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/BAAI/Chinese-LiPS
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15066
  The dataset card declares CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0. No dataset videos or reference labels
  are bundled in this repository. Source attribution and license remain in the
  downloaded manifests; partial archive retrieval does not verify the whole archive.
- scripts/train_chinese_adapter.py is a separately written, optional CNVSRC
  encoder adaptation experiment. Its base weights and resulting partial tensors
  retain the source research restrictions described below. No automatic product
  activation or redistribution of source weights is performed.
- scripts/train_chinese_joint_adapter.py, scripts/compare_chinese_decoders.py,
  scripts/compare_chinese_reports.py and scripts/analyze_chinese_errors.py extend
  the separate CNVSRC research entry with train/dev-only adaptation, decoder
  comparison, frozen paired evaluation and analysis of saved reports. They do not
  install a model into the GUI. Source weights and derived adaptation tensors retain
  the author's research/benchmarking restrictions; downloaded Chinese-LiPS material
  retains CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0. This repository distributes code, protocols and aggregate
  results, not weights, adapters, videos, per-clip references/manifests or raw predictions.
  中文：上述工具属于独立的 CNVSRC 研究入口，不会自动将模型安装到 GUI。
  基座权重与派生适配参数仍受作者研究/基准比较用途限制；下载的 Chinese-LiPS
  材料保留 CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0。仓库仅提供代码、协议和汇总结果，不上传权重、
  适配器、视频、逐条参考文本/清单或原始预测。
- The optional CMLR visual checkpoint and Chinese language model are downloaded from the
  original author's published model zoo, not bundled or redistributed here:
  https://github.com/mpc001/Visual_Speech_Recognition_for_Multiple_Languages#model-zoo
  Their source project license restricts use to research/private study and comparative
  prototypes, excluding commercial product development:
  https://github.com/mpc001/Visual_Speech_Recognition_for_Multiple_Languages/blob/master/LICENSE
  CMLR dataset use is also research-only: https://www.vipazoo.cn/CMLR.html
  No additional code is copied from that source project by this adaptation.
- scripts/evaluate_cnvsrc.py is an optional, separately written pure-visual research
  comparison adapter using the existing Apache-licensed ESPnet modules. It uses
  verified functional architecture parameters and reads the vocabulary from the author's pinned
  CNVSRC2025 sources and requires separately downloaded weights; it does not import
  or redistribute the author's source code, vocabulary files or model weights:
  https://github.com/liu12366262626/CNVSRC2025/tree/main/VSR
  https://github.com/liu12366262626/CNVSRC2025/blob/main/VSR/LICENSE
  https://huggingface.co/ReflectionL/CNVSRC2025Baseline
  Their research/benchmarking restrictions are not a commercial product license.
- Optional Chinese quiet-speech inference uses faster-whisper (MIT), CTranslate2 and
  OpenCC-Python (Apache 2.0), installed as dependencies. Whisper model weights are downloaded
  separately via faster-whisper; check the selected model card. Default model conversion:
  https://huggingface.co/dropbox-dash/faster-whisper-large-v3-turbo
  This audio backend is not a Mandarin visual/AVSR model.
